  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The formula measures pair freshness, not witness freshness: when j<i, max(i,j)=i, so an arbitrarily old witness receives no additional age penalty relative to a newer witness preceding the same anchor. Rename the mechanism or justify this asymmetry.",
    "The proposed comparisons do not isolate corroboration freshness from stronger recency weighting and reduced residual strength. Add a matched anchor-decay control and report support mass, clipping frequency, and residual norms.",
    "An efficient implementation is unspecified. The reference loops cost O(BL³) before embedding pooling. For a fixed retained window, support can instead update as s[t,i]=max(exp(-1/rho_witness)*s[t-1,i], S[i,t]) for existing anchors, with separately initialized new anchors and eligibility masks. Sliding-window expiration requires additional handling.",
    "Reproduction still requires executable baseline integration, an unambiguous inherited TF–IDF configuration and token pattern, resolved training/checkpoint settings, predictor signatures, and a prespecified budget allocation. Initial prediction parity also requires preserving baseline initialization and random-number consumption.",
    "No validation results establish that stale corroboration is a material failure mode. Positional age cannot measure elapsed-time staleness or seasonality. Lexical duplicates, boilerplate, repeated historical positions, and metadata coverage remain possible shortcuts.",
    "Originality 4 and potential 7 are provisional judgments without direct temporal-recommendation comparisons or validation evidence. Difficulty 4 appears optimistic for complete training, sparse text processing, diagnostics, and predictor integration."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Check whether the temporal operator offers anything beyond established time weighting and identify controls that distinguish pair freshness from stronger anchor recency.",
      "query": "In sequential recommendation, how do TiSASRec, time-aware attention, and exponential-decay item-history pooling distinguish event recency, pairwise temporal distance, and recurring-interest freshness? Find equations and ablations relevant to a SASRec residual with weight exp(-(t-i)/rho_anchor) * max_j[S(i,j) * exp(-(t-max(i,j))/rho_witness)]."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve implementation complexity before assigning training allocations or claiming low implementation difficulty.",
      "query": "What exact streaming algorithms compute exponentially decayed running maxima with eligibility masks and sliding-window expiration? Consider causal sequential recommendation support s[t,i]=max over j<=t of S(i,j)*exp(-(t-max(i,j))/rho), excluding identical item IDs and position gaps below three. Explain fixed-window recurrences, new-anchor initialization, expiration, numerical stability, and time/memory complexity."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Find evidence and experimental controls for lexical shortcuts and weak recurrence coverage before interpreting any validation gain as improved temporal evidence.",
      "query": "In Amazon sequential recommendation using item-title and description TF-IDF, what studies examine duplicate descriptions, brand boilerplate, metadata missingness, and popularity as sources of apparent semantic improvement? Look for matched text-permutation, duplicate-group exclusion, recency-only, and residual-magnitude controls that can separate lexical recurrence from these shortcuts."
    }
  ]
